; DOMAIN: borcherds-lift [CLOSED, derived 2026-07-25]
; Claim: The Borcherds singular theta lift sends a weakly holomorphic vector-valued modular form of weight 1-n/2 to a meromorphic modular form (Borcherds product) on an orthogonal Shimura variety O(n,2), whose divisor is an explicit integral combination of special (Heegner) divisors. This gives a geometric/automorphic realization of the Kudla generating series: the special-divisor coefficients organized by the input form's principal part reproduce the weight-3/2 (GKZ, 143) and higher Siegel (kudla_program, 144) generating series as actual divisors of modular forms, while the Kudla-Rapoport (145) local densities control their arithmetic intersection. Bridge: genesis_kudla_rapoport (local arithmetic densities of the same special cycles) + genesis_kudla_program (global generating-series framework realized geometrically here) + genesis_gross_kohnen (weight-3/2 divisor antecedent) + genesis_waldspurger (theta-lift/period companion).
(= (borcherds-lift $f) (meromorphic-modular-form (orthogonal-shimura (signature $n 2)) (divisor (heegner-divisor-combination (principal-part $f)))))
(= (borcherds-realizes-kudla $V) (implies (weakly-holomorphic-input $f) (equal (divisor (borcherds-lift $f)) (kudla-generating-series $V))))
(= (borcherds-product-expansion $f) (infinite-product (lambda ($lambda) (exponent (fourier-coefficient $f $lambda)))))